{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 4, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "f_fx and g_fx are equal on the domain of f_fx (sampled, not proved; SAT gave up on 1501 AIG nodes within its budget of 100000 conflicts or 100000000 steps)\n  polynomials of total degree at most 10, equal at 4 random points mod 2^61 - 1: two that differ agree at one with probability at most 10/(2^61 - 1) = 4.34e-18 (Schwartz-Zippel), at all 4 with at most 3.54e-70: equal over the integers except with that probability, and then for every input here (a probabilistic answer, not a proof)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 4, "ok": true, "cmd": "equiv", "ucas": "equiv f_fx g_fx", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "equiv", "equal": true, "exhaustive": false, "mismatch_points": 0, "method": "sampled", "sat": {"result": "gave_up", "aig_nodes": 1501}, "identity_test": {"result": "equal_probably", "error_probability": 3.5373746401666845e-70}}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "proof": {"kind": "numeric", "text": "sampled, not proved; SAT gave up on 1501 AIG nodes within its budget of 100000 conflicts or 100000000 steps"}, "files": [], "text": "f_fx and g_fx are equal on the domain of f_fx (sampled, not proved; SAT gave up on 1501 AIG nodes within its budget of 100000 conflicts or 100000000 steps)\n  polynomials of total degree at most 10, equal at 4 random points mod 2^61 - 1: two that differ agree at one with probability at most 10/(2^61 - 1) = 4.34e-18 (Schwartz-Zippel), at all 4 with at most 3.54e-70: equal over the integers except with that probability, and then for every input here (a probabilistic answer, not a proof)\n"}, "isError": false}}
